    "OVERRIDES: OTHER BLOCKS WHERE THE STREAM IS A CERTAIN WAY.",
    "An override is a sticker on its ring. 'when' lists stream properties; all of them must hold. Values run 0 to 1:",
    "slope 0 flat .. 1 sheer (0.05 gentle, 0.2 brisk, 0.5 steep). width 0 = a 1-block brook .. 1 = a 32-block river.",
    "speed 0 still .. 1 the fastest. bend 0 straight .. 1 a hairpin (0.2 = a clear curve). side: inner or outer of a bend.",
    "to_mouth and to_junction: 0 at the sea or lake, or at a confluence; 1 = 16 stream widths away or more.",
    "flat_run: 0 just below a steep part .. 1 a long, settled flat.",
    "Comparisons: > 0.3, >= 0.3, < 0.3, <= 0.3. fade: how softly the sticker comes in. At the threshold it takes",
    "half the blocks, and all of them 'fade' past it (default 0.1).",
    "The mod tries the overrides top to bottom; the first one that succeeds paints. Put the most specific first.",
    "An override can set its own pattern and scale. If it does not, it uses the ring's."
  ],
  "biomes": ["minecraft:old_growth_pine_taiga", "minecraft:old_growth_spruce_taiga"],
  "bed": {
    "block": ["minecraft:gravel", "minecraft:gravel", "minecraft:cobblestone"],
    "overrides": [
      { "when": { "bend": "> 0.2", "side": "inner" }, "block": "minecraft:sand" },
      { "when": { "to_junction": "< 0.15" }, "block": ["minecraft:gravel", "minecraft:sand"], "pattern": "speckle" },
      { "when": { "flat_run": ">= 0.6", "speed": "< 0.3" }, "fade": 0.2, "block": ["minecraft:mud", "minecraft:clay"], "scale": 60 }
    ]
  },
  "waterline": {
    "block": "minecraft:coarse_dirt",
    "overrides": [
      { "when": { "speed": "> 0.6" }, "block": "minecraft:mossy_cobblestone" }
    ]
  },
  "bank": {
    "block": ["minecraft:podzol", "streamsreflowing:chameleon"],
    "overrides": [
      { "when": { "slope": "> 0.4" }, "fade": 0.15, "block": ["minecraft:stone", "minecraft:andesite", "minecraft:tuff"] },
      { "when": { "bend": "> 0.25", "side": "outer" }, "block": "minecraft:rooted_dirt" },
      { "when": { "width": "<= 0.1" }, "block": "minecraft:moss_block" },
      { "when": { "to_mouth": "< 0.2" }, "block": ["minecraft:sand", "minecraft:coarse_dirt"] }
    ]
  }
}

configs.streamsreflowing/bank_styles/examples/05:
{
  "_about": [
    "SCENERY ON A RING: FALLEN LOGS ON THE BANK, STUMPS ON THE TOP BANK.",
    "A ring's 'features' names bank feature DEFINITIONS, not placed features. A definition is a file in",
    "config/streamsreflowing/bank_features/ with a 'features' list and no biomes or tags. Its id is its file name.",
    "This style uses two. Copy riverside_logs.json and riverside_stumps.json from bank_features/examples/ into",
    "bank_features/ as well, or the rings have nothing to place.",
    "In a datapack a definition is data/<namespace>/streamsreflowing/bank_feature/<name>.json, and its id is <namespace>:<name>.",
    "chance: the percent of the bank sites the mod samples in that ring that get one. Keep it low, 1 to 5."
  ],
  "biomes": ["minecraft:dark_forest"],
  "bed": ["minecraft:mud", "minecraft:gravel"],
  "waterline": "minecraft:rooted_dirt",
  "bank": {
    "reach": 60,
    "block": ["minecraft:podzol", "streamsreflowing:chameleon"],
    "features": [ { "id": "riverside_logs", "chance": 3 } ]
  },
  "top_bank": {
    "block": ["streamsreflowing:chameleon", "minecraft:air"],
    "features": [ { "id": "riverside_stumps", "chance": 2 } ]
  }
}

configs.streamsreflowing/bank_styles/examples/07:
{
  "_about": [
    "LEAVE A BIOME'S STREAMS RAW.",
    "enabled: false still wins the biome, then paints nothing: the carved ground stays as the terrain made it.",
    "To keep only one ring natural instead, give that ring minecraft:air, for example \"bank\": \"minecraft:air\"."
  ],
  "biomes": ["minecraft:mushroom_fields"],
  "enabled": false
}

configs.tectonic.json:
{
  "biomes": {
    "temperature_multiplier": 1.0,
    "temperature_offset": 0.0,
    "temperature_scale": 0.25,
    "vegetation_multiplier": 1.0,
    "vegetation_offset": 0.0,
    "vegetation_scale": 0.25
  },
  "caves": {
    // Whether old caves/ravines should generate. Game restart required!
    "carvers_enabled": true,
    // Density added to cheese caves. Lower values = bigger cheese caves.
    "cheese_additive": 0.27,
    // The standard expansive, large cheese-shaped caves.
    "cheese_enabled": true,
    // The distance in depth between the start and end of the depth cutoff. 0.1 means caves close over ~12 blocks, 0.0 means caves cut off at the `depth_cutoff_start` value immediately.
    "depth_cutoff_size": 0.1,
    // The depth noise value that caves stop generating. 0.1 cuts off caves ~12 blocks below the surface, 0.5 cuts off caves ~64 blocks below the surface.
    "depth_cutoff_start": 0.1,
    // Density added to noodle caves. Lower values = bigger noodle caves.
    "noodle_additive": -0.075,
    // The narrow, claustrophobic noodle-shaped caves.
    "noodle_enabled": true,
    // Alters ore generation to generate at more acceptable levels when min_y is lowered.
    "ore_fix": false,
    // The tunneling, medium sized spaghetti-shaped caves.
    "spaghetti_enabled": true
  },
  "continents": {
    // Horizontally scales continents. Lower values = larger continents and oceans between them.
    "continents_scale": 0.13,
    // Horizontally scales erosion, primarily impacting mountains. Lower values = thicker mountain ranges and terrain between them.
    "erosion_scale": 0.25,
    // The threshold where plateau terrain becomes flatter terrain. Positive numbers favor flat terrain and negative numbers favor plateau terrain.
    "flat_terrain_skew": 0.1,
    // Some jungles generate massive pillars that can extend upwards of a hundred blocks tall.
    "jungle_pillars": true,
    // Skews terrain towards or away from oceans. Lower values = more oceans. Above -0.45, deep oceans will not spawn! Above -0.2, oceans will not spawn!
    "ocean_offset": -0.8,
    // Horizontally scales the ridge noise, primarily impacting rivers and terrain around them like plateaus. Lower values = wider rivers and terrain between them.
    "ridge_scale": 0.25,
    // Underground rivers under snowy biomes will generate with ice.
    "river_ice": false,
    // Underground rivers will rarely generate with hanging lanterns.
    "river_lanterns": true,
    // Some Plains biomes generate very smooth, hilly terrain.
    "rolling_hills": true,
    // Rivers that reach mountain ranges continue underground, allowing smoother boat exploration.
    "underground_rivers": true
  },
  "experimental": {
    "alternate_continents_scaling": false,
    "alternate_erosion_scaling": false
  },
  "general": {
    // When disabled, the mod lays dormant and does nothing. Game restart required!
    "mod_enabled": true,
    // Offsets the y-level snow in cold biomes like Taigas starts at.
    "snow_start_offset": 128
  },
  "global_terrain": {
    // Increases the effects of Vertical Scale on mountainous terrain. This will increase the scale of mountains and plateaus faster than lowlands.
    "elevation_boost": 0.0,
    // Rare, deep underground tunnels of lava sometimes generate at the bottom of the world.
    "lava_tunnels": true,
    "max_y": 320,
    "min_y": -64,
    // Greatly smoothens out the terrain like Tectonic v2, removing staircasing artifacts at the cost of strange/broken generation in deep oceans and windswept biomes.
    "ultrasmooth": false,
    // Vertically stretches terrain above sea level. Doubling this value will double the surface's height at a given point from sea level.
    "vertical_scale": 1.125
  },
  "islands": {
    "enabled": true,
    "noise_multiplier": 1.0,
    "noise_offset": 0.0,
    "noise_scale": 0.11
  },
  "minor_version": 1,
  "oceans": {
    // 0 is at sea level, -0.5 is 64 blocks below sea level.
    "deep_ocean_depth": -0.45,
    // Offsets (vanilla) ocean monuments to adjust for deeper oceans.
    "monument_offset": -30,
    // 0 is at sea level, -0.5 is 64 blocks below sea level.
    "ocean_depth": -0.22,
    // Removes the surface ice from Frozen Oceans, making them as navigable as Deep Frozen Oceans.
    "remove_frozen_ocean_ice": false
  }
}

